### Section 2 Stated Questions & Q1: Premise Audit

#### Q1(a) & Section 2 Question 2: Is `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` the only code the BL rule must exempt at HEAD?
- **Verdict**: **TRUE (`READ` / `REASONED`)**.
- **Census of `EXPEVT_*` definitions ([sh4_exception.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/sh4_exception.h#L57-L76))**:
  - Reset-category codes defined: `EXPEVT_RESET_POWER` (`0x000`), `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` (`0x020`), `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` (`0x140`).
  - General-exception codes defined: `EXPEVT_TLB_MISS_LD` (`0x040`), `EXPEVT_TLB_MISS_ST` (`0x060`), `EXPEVT_TLB_MOD` (`0x080`), `EXPEVT_TLB_PROT_LD` (`0x0a0`), `EXPEVT_TLB_PROT_ST` (`0x0c0`), `EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_LD` (`0x0e0`), `EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_ST` (`0x100`), `EXPEVT_FPU` (`0x120`), `EXPEVT_TRAPA` (`0x160`), `EXPEVT_RES_INST` (`0x180`), `EXPEVT_SLOT_INST` (`0x1a0`), `EXPEVT_BREAK` (`0x1e0`), `EXPEVT_FPU_DISABLE` (`0x800`), `EXPEVT_FPU_SLOT_DISABLE` (`0x820`).
- **Exhaustive census of every [`sh_exception()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L906) call site across `GXEMUL-SEC/src` (`READ`)**:
  1. [cpu_dyntrans.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c#L250): `sh_exception(cpu, 0, cpu->cd.sh.int_to_assert, 0)` — interrupt delivery (`expevt = 0`, `intevt > 0`).
  2. [dev_sh4.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sh4.c#L1304-L1305): `sh_exception(cpu, EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT, 0, 0)` — UTLB associative write with `n_hits > 1`. (ITLB multiple-hit is not implemented per [`sh_translate_v2p()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_sh.c#L151), and shares `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT = 0x140`.)
  3. [memory_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_sh.c#L249) and [memory_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_sh.c#L368-L369): raises `EXPEVT_TLB_MISS_LD` (`0x040`), `EXPEVT_TLB_MISS_ST` (`0x060`), `EXPEVT_TLB_MOD` (`0x080`), `EXPEVT_TLB_PROT_LD` (`0x0a0`), `EXPEVT_TLB_PROT_ST` (`0x0c0`).
  4. [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c): raises `EXPEVT_RES_INST` (`0x180` at `:53`, `:245`, `:3212`, `:3237`, `:3294`, `:3713`), `EXPEVT_SLOT_INST` (`0x1a0` at `:2853`, `:3210`, `:3235`, `:3292`), `EXPEVT_FPU_SLOT_DISABLE` (`0x820` at `:62`), `EXPEVT_FPU_DISABLE` (`0x800` at `:64`), `EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_LD` (`0x0e0` at `:212`), `EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_ST` (`0x100` at `:218`), `EXPEVT_TRAPA` (`0x160` at `:2858`).
- Neither `EXPEVT_RESET_POWER` (`0x000`), `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` (`0x020`), `EXPEVT_FPU` (`0x120`), nor `EXPEVT_BREAK` (`0x1e0`) is ever passed to `sh_exception(..., intevt=0, ...)`. Thus `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` (`0x140`) is the only non-general code reachable at `sh_exception()` with `intevt == 0`.

#### Section 2 Question 1: Module reset effects (SH7750 Manual 5.5.3)
- **Verdict**: **CONFIRMED OUT OF SCOPE (`READ`)**.
- In [`sh_exception()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L1024-L1030) (brief `:1015-1021`), the reset `case` arm (`EXPEVT_RESET_POWER` / `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` / `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT`) sets `cpu->pc = 0xa0000000; cpu->cd.sh.vbr = 0;` and updates `sr`, without resetting any peripheral module registers in [dev_sh4.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sh4.c). Disclosing that module-register reset is unmodelled for all reset paths in `sh_exception()` is accurate and appropriate.

#### Q1(b): Does any committed row or guest path depend on `H'000` being latched on this path?
- **Verdict**: **NO (`READ` / `REASONED`)**.
- Cold boot in [`sh_cpu_new()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L77-L255) leaves `cpu->cd.sh.expevt` at `0x000` (`EXPEVT_RESET_POWER`) by zero-initialization without calling `sh_exception()`.
- In [sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L173-L221), `tlbm single` checks `expevt == 0x00000000`, which is that untouched cold-boot initial value (no exception fires on a single hit). None of the 6 committed rows sets `SR.BL`.

#### Q1(c): Is the user-break sentence right (no raiser)?
- **Verdict**: **TRUE that `EXPEVT_BREAK` has no raiser in `src/`, WITH A COMMENT REFINEMENT (`READ` / `REASONED`)**.
- `EXPEVT_BREAK` (`0x1e0`) is defined at [sh4_exception.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/sh4_exception.h#L73) and never referenced anywhere in `GXEMUL-SEC/src/`; the UBC region (`0xff200000..0xff200023`) in [`dev_sh4_access()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sh4.c#L2024-L2037) is a stub (`/* TODO */`). Furthermore, `switch (expevt)` in [`sh_exception()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L968-L1034) has no `case EXPEVT_BREAK:` and would hit `default: exit(1)`.
- Architecturally, a user break when `SR.BL == 1` is suppressed at the UBC rather than delivered through `sh_exception()` as an exempted `EXPEVT_BREAK` (as the working-tree comment at [cpu_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L920-L922) rightly states, improving on the Pass-1 brief's draft comment).

#### Q1(d): Do interrupts truly never reach the block — and is the brief's walkthrough of `intevt > 0` right?
- **Verdict**: **Interrupts never reach `sh_exception()` with `BL=1` (`READ`), Set-aside: the parenthetical claim in `Q1(d)` of the brief gets the `intevt > 0` dataflow backwards (`READ` / `REASONED`)**.
- **Why interrupts never reach `sh_exception()` with `BL=1` (`READ`)**:
  - The only call site with `intevt > 0` is [cpu_dyntrans.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c#L247-L250), gated by `if (cpu->cd.sh.int_to_assert > 0 && !(cpu->cd.sh.sr & SH_SR_BL) && ...)` (and [`X(sleep)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L259-L261) checks the same condition before waking).
- **Correction to `Q1(d)`'s parenthetical (`READ` / `REASONED`)**:
  - `Q1(d)` in [brief_shblreset_p1.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w577/brief_shblreset_p1.md#L211-L213) states: *(the `intevt > 0` path sets `expevt = -1` AFTER the block -- walk it: an interrupt delivered with BL set would be rewritten too, so the `cpu_dyntrans.c` gate is load-bearing)*.
  - Walk [`sh_exception()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L910-L972) (brief `:910-963`) if called with `expevt = 0, intevt > 0` while `SR.BL == 1`:
    1. At `:910-927`, the `BL` block prints `fatal("[ sh_exception(): BL bit already set. ]\n")` and rewrites local variable `expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` (or `EXPEVT_RESET_POWER` at HEAD).
    2. At `:954-959` (brief `:945-950`):
       ```c
       if (intevt > 0) {
           cpu->cd.sh.intevt = intevt;
           expevt = -1;
       } else {
           cpu->cd.sh.expevt = expevt;
       }
       ```
    3. Because `intevt > 0` runs **after** the `BL` block, `cpu->cd.sh.expevt` is **not** written, and local `expevt` is **overwritten with `-1`**, discarding the `BL` block's rewrite! Then `switch (expevt)` at `:968` takes `case -1:` (`cpu->pc = cpu->cd.sh.vbr + 0x600; break;`).
  - Therefore, the `cpu_dyntrans.c:247` gate is load-bearing to prevent an interrupt from being *delivered* (and printing `fatal`) while `BL=1`, **not** because the `BL` block's `expevt` rewrite would survive on the `intevt > 0` path. The working-tree comment at [cpu_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L922-L924) (*"and the intevt path below discards expevt before storing it"*) already fixes this.

#### Q1(e): Are the witness rows' instruction encodings and `want` values right?
- **Verdict**: **TRUE (`READ` / `MEASURED`)**.
- Verified against the decoder in [`sh_instr_to_be_translated()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4170-L5060), the executor in [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c), and the recorded artifacts [witness_head.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/witness_20261102/witness_head.out#L1-L12) and [witness_fixed.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/witness_fixed.out#L1-L12):
  - `TRAPA_1 = 0xc301`: `main_opcode = 0xc`, `r8 = 0x3`, `lo8 = 0x01`, decoded at [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4864-L4867) to [`X(trapa)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L2848-L2859), which writes `TRA = 0x04` and calls `sh_exception(cpu, EXPEVT_TRAPA, 0, 0)` (`0x160`). With `BL=1`, `want`: `expevt = 0x00000020`, `pc = 0xa0000000`. With `BL=0` (`tlbm trapa`), `want`: `expevt = 0x00000160`.
  - `MOV_L_R0_AT_R1 = 0x2102`, `MOV_L_R4_AT_R5 = 0x2542`, `MOV_L_R6_AT_R7 = 0x2762`: `mov.l rM,@rN` (`0010 nnnn mmmm 0010`), decoded at [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4298-L4300) to [`X(mov_l_store_rm_rn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L1408-L1432). Stores `PTEH` to UTLB entry 0 (`0xf6000000`) and entry 1 (`0xf6000100`), then writes `ASSOC` (`0xf6000080`), firing `sh_exception(cpu, EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT, 0, 0)` (`0x140`) at [dev_sh4.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sh4.c#L1304-L1305). With `BL=1`, `want`: `expevt = 0x00000140`, `pc = 0xa0000000`.
  - `MOV_L_AT_R1_R2 = 0x6212` (in the working-tree [sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L229)): `mov.l @r1,r2` (`0110 0010 0001 0010`) with `r1 = 0x8c010001`, decoded at [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L4649-L4651) to [`X(load_l_rm_rn)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L739-L764), which invokes [`SH_ALIGN_CHECK_LD(addr, 3)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L209-L214) and calls `sh_exception(cpu, EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_LD, 0, addr)` (`0x0e0`). With `BL=1`, `want`: `expevt = 0x00000020`.

