### Q2: The Partition (`READ` / `REASONED`)

Over the $4 \times 2$ product `{general exception, TLB multiple hit, interrupt, user break} x {BL clear, BL set}` at [`sh_exception()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L906-L1035):

| Event Category | `SR.BL == 0` (`BL` clear) | `SR.BL == 1` (`BL` set) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **General exception** (`0x040..0x100`, `0x160..0x1a0`, `0x800`, `0x820`) | **Unchanged** by fix: latches `expevt` as-is; vectors to `vbr + 0x100` (or `vbr + 0x400` for TLB miss).<br>**Probe coverage**: None in the 6 committed HEAD rows! Covered once working-tree row `tlbm trapa` (`0x160`) is included. | **Changed** by fix: `expevt` rewritten to `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` (`0x020`) instead of `EXPEVT_RESET_POWER` (`0x000`); vectors to `0xa0000000` with `vbr = 0`.<br>**Probe coverage**: `tlbm bl trapa` (`0x160`) and `tlbm bl ldmis` (`0x0e0`). |
| **TLB multiple hit** (`EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT = 0x140`) | **Unchanged** by fix: latches `0x140`; vectors to `0xa0000000` with `vbr = 0`.<br>**Probe coverage**: Committed rows `tlbm alive`, `tlbm expevt`, `tlbm pc`, `tlbm vbr`, `tlbm sr`. | **Changed** by fix: exempted from rewrite, so `expevt` stays `0x140` (instead of being clobbered to `0x000`); vectors to `0xa0000000` with `vbr = 0`.<br>**Probe coverage**: `tlbm bl mhit` (`0x140`). |
| **Interrupt** (`intevt > 0`, `expevt = 0`) | **Unchanged** by fix: latches `intevt`, sets `expevt = -1`, vectors to `vbr + 0x600`.<br>**Probe coverage**: Covered by `sh_intprio_probe.py`. | **Unreachable** at `sh_exception()`: blocked by `!(cpu->cd.sh.sr & SH_SR_BL)` at [cpu_dyntrans.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c#L247) and [cpu_sh_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L260) (and if entered directly, `intevt > 0` overwrites `expevt = -1` at [cpu_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L956)). |
| **User break** (`EXPEVT_BREAK = 0x1e0`) | **Unreachable** in this tree: `EXPEVT_BREAK` has no raiser in `src/`, UBC at [dev_sh4.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sh4.c#L2024-L2037) is a stub, and `switch (expevt)` has no `case EXPEVT_BREAK:`. | **Unreachable** in this tree (and suppressed at the UBC on hardware when `BL=1`). |

