| **(b)** `if (sr & SH_SR_BL)` block deleted (or rewrite removed) | **No** | Any general exception with `BL=1` (`expevt = 0x160`): leaves `expevt = 0x160` and vectors to `vbr + 0x100` instead of `0xa0000000`. (`tlbm bl mhit` stays green.) | `tlbm bl trapa` (`got 0x160`, `want 0x020`), `tlbm bl ldmis` (`got 0x0e0`, `want 0x020`) | **Floor** (clause (c): identity body) |
| **(c)** `expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL;` (exemption removed) | **No** | `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` (`0x140`) with `BL=1`: rewrites `0x140` to `0x020`. | `tlbm bl mhit` (`got 0x020`, `want 0x140`) | **Floor** (clause (d): predicate dropped to `true`) |
| **(d)** `if (expevt != EXPEVT_TRAPA) expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL;` (wrong code exempted) | **No** | Both `EXPEVT_TRAPA` (`0x160` left as `0x160`) and `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` (`0x140` rewritten to `0x020`) with `BL=1`. | `tlbm bl trapa` (`got 0x160`, `want 0x020`) **and** `tlbm bl mhit` (`got 0x020`, `want 0x140`) | **Floor** (clause (d): predicate corrupted) |
| **(e)** Exemption widened to `expevt < 0x100` (or `expevt < 0x100 \|\| expevt == 0x140`) | **No** (see note below on `0x040..0x0e0` vs. `{0x000, 0x020}`) |- If written `if (expevt >= 0x100) expevt = 0x020;`: differs on `0x140` (rewritten to `0x020`) **and** on general codes `0x040..0x0e0` (left unrewritten).<br>- If written `if (expevt >= 0x100 && expevt != 0x140) expevt = 0x020;`: differs on general codes `0x040..0x0e0` (`TLB_MISS_LD/ST`, `TLB_MOD`, `TLB_PROT_LD/ST`, `ADDR_ERR_LD`). | - First form reds `tlbm bl mhit` (`got 0x020`) and `tlbm bl ldmis` (`got 0x0e0`).<br>- Second form **escapes** the Pass-1 2-row table (`TRAPA` is `0x160 >= 0x100`), but **reds** `tlbm bl ldmis` (`0x0e0 < 0x100`: `got 0x0e0`, `want 0x020`)! | **Floor** once `tlbm bl ldmis` (`0x0e0`) is in the table; see note below for `{0x000, 0x020}` |
| **(f)** `if (expevt == EXPEVT_TRAPA) expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL;` | **No** | Any non-`TRAPA` general exception with `BL=1` (e.g. `EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_LD = 0x0e0` or `EXPEVT_RES_INST = 0x180`): leaves `expevt` unrewritten and takes the general vector. | **Escapes** the Pass-1 2-row table; **reds** `tlbm bl ldmis` (`got 0x0e0`, `want 0x020`) in the working-tree 10-row table. | **Floor** on `(f)` once `tlbm bl ldmis` rides; **Clause (e)** disclosure for the remaining 10 undriven general codes |

- **Important check on `Q3(e)`'s premise (`READ` / `REASONED`)**:
  - `Q3(e)` in [brief_shblreset_p1.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w577/brief_shblreset_p1.md#L221-L222) describes `expevt < 0x100` as *"every reset-category code"*. That is **false** in SuperH encoding ([sh4_exception.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/sh4_exception.h#L57-L68)):
    1. Only `0x000` (`EXPEVT_RESET_POWER`) and `0x020` (`EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL`) are $< \text{0x100}$ reset codes; `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` is `0x140` ($\ge \text{0x100}$).
    2. Codes `0x040`, `0x060`, `0x080`, `0x0a0`, `0x0c0`, and `0x0e0` are **general exceptions** (`TLB_MISS_LD`, `TLB_MISS_ST`, `TLB_MOD`, `TLB_PROT_LD`, `TLB_PROT_ST`, `ADDR_ERR_LD`), all of which are $< \text{0x100}$ and all of which have active raisers in `memory_sh.c` / `cpu_sh_instr.c`!
  - By contrast, if a mutant widens the exemption strictly to the true reset-category codes `{0x000, 0x020, 0x140}` (`expevt != 0x140 && expevt > 0x020`), that mutant **is** strictly equivalent in this tree because `0x000` and `0x020` have no `intevt == 0` callers to `sh_exception()`.
- **Should a second general-code row ride?**
  - **YES (`REASONED`)**: The working tree's `tlbm bl ldmis` ([sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L228-L231), 1-step misaligned load `mov.l @r1,r2` at `CODE + 1` raising `EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_LD = 0x0e0`) simultaneously kills `(f)` (`expevt == EXPEVT_TRAPA`) **and** kills the `< 0x100` exemption widening in `(e)` (`0x0e0 < 0x100`). The remaining 10 reachable general codes (`0x040..0x0c0`, `0x100`, `0x180`, `0x1a0`, `0x800`, `0x820`) are then cleanly disclosed under Clause (e).

