### Q4: Option-Set Completeness & Unlatched `fatal()` (`READ` / `REASONED`)

- **Option-set completeness**: **COMPLETE (`READ` / `REASONED`)**. Both hardware deviations in [`sh_exception()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L910-L927) under `SR.BL == 1` (wrong reset constant `0x000` vs. `0x020` for general exceptions, and missing exemption for `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT = 0x140`) are completely resolved by the 2-line fix. Notice that the downstream `switch (expevt)` at [cpu_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L1024-L1030) already groups `EXPEVT_RESET_POWER`, `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL`, and `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` into the exact same reset vector arm (`cpu->pc = 0xa0000000; cpu->cd.sh.vbr = 0;`).
- **Should the unlatched `fatal("[ sh_exception(): BL bit already set. ]\n")` at `:911` be latched `(once)` in this round?**
  - **NO — leave it to `floodclass` ([OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L24144)) (`REASONED`)**:
    1. It is a diagnostic-rate concern (`floodclass`), orthogonal to the `EXPEVT` value fix in `#577`.
    2. Note also for `floodclass` when it arrives: `fatal("[ sh_exception(): BL bit already set. ]\n")` at `:911` currently fires even when `expevt == EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT`, where `BL` being set is *not* what escalates the exception to reset (TLB multiple-hit is already a reset exception regardless of `BL`). Both the `(once)` latch and whether the message should be gated on `expevt != EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` belong in `floodclass`.

