### Q5: The Vehicle ([sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py) & [gate_sh_rounding.sh](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh)) (`READ` / `REASONED` / `MEASURED`)

1. **Do any of the 6 committed rows re-pin under the fix?**
   - **NO (`READ` / `MEASURED`)**.
   - At cold reset in [`sh_cpu_new()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L123), `cpu->cd.sh.sr = SH_SR_MD | SH_SR_IMASK` (`0x400000f0`, so `BL = 0` and `RB = 0`). [`sh_ipl_g_emul_init()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/promemul/sh_ipl_g.c#L52-L67) sets `vbr = 0x8c000000` and does not touch `sr`.
   - Committed rows `tlbm alive`, `tlbm expevt`, `tlbm pc`, `tlbm vbr`, and `tlbm single` ([sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L202-L221)) run with that default `sr = 0x400000f0` (`BL = 0`); `tlbm sr` pre-sets `sr=0x40008000` (`MD | FD`, `BL = 0`).
   - Thus none of the 6 committed rows enters `sh_exception()` with `SR.BL` set, and all 6 produce identical values before and after the fix.

2. **Is the `sr=0x500000f0` pre-set right (RB clear, so the program's bank-0 seeds are the ones the stores use)?**
   - **YES (`READ` / `REASONED`)**, and the underlying debugger mechanism is worth noting:
   - `0x500000f0` is `SH_SR_MD (0x40000000) | SH_SR_BL (0x10000000) | SH_SR_IMASK (0x000000f0)`, with `SH_SR_RB (0x20000000)` **clear** (bank 0).
   - In the GXemul debugger, `sr=0x500000f0` executes [`debugger_assignment()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger.c#L540-L579) $\to$ [`debugger_parse_name()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_expr.c#L164-L173) $\to$ `settings_access()`, which writes directly to the `uint32_t` field registered by [`CPU_SETTINGS_ADD_REGISTER32("sr", cpu->cd.sh.sr)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L129) **without** calling [`sh_update_sr()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L846-L860).
   - Because `cpu->cd.sh.sr` starts at `0x400000f0` (`RB = 0`, bank 0 active in `r[0..7]`), keeping `RB = 0` in `0x500000f0` ensures `cpu->cd.sh.sr`'s `RB` bit stays synchronized with the active bank-0 registers (`r0`, `r1`, `r4`, `r5`, `r6`, `r7`) during the 3 store instructions, **and** ensures that when [`sh_exception()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L961-L962) subsequently calls `sh_update_sr(cpu, cpu->cd.sh.sr | SH_SR_MD | SH_SR_RB | SH_SR_BL)`, `(new_sr & SH_SR_RB) != (old_sr & SH_SR_RB)` evaluates true (`1 != 0`) and swaps `r[0..7]` with `r_bank[0..7]`. (If `sr=...` had set `RB = 1` via direct `settings_access` write, `sh_update_sr()` on exception entry would see `old_sr & SH_SR_RB` already `1` and skip the bank swap!)

3. **Gate alignment check ([gate_sh_rounding.sh](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh#L254-L259)) (`READ` / `REASONED`)**:
   - As detailed in Change 1 at the top, [gate_sh_rounding.sh](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh#L254-L259) checks `n=$(count "$TMLOG" "^$v  .*ok$")` (two spaces after `$v`), while [`check()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L88) formats `name` with `%-14s`. Therefore row names must be $\le 13$ chars (`tlbm bl trapa`, `tlbm bl mhit`, `tlbm bl ldmis`, `tlbm trapa`), and [gate_sh_rounding.sh](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_sh_rounding.sh#L254-L259) must be updated from `6` to `10` rows with those exact 4 names added to the `for v in ...` loop.

